/-!
# Extending recognized component sections in 13.8.5

`complete_conclusions_of_recognized_section` proves the conditional passage
from a specified component with its literal natural section to all three
conclusions of 13.8.5. Its inputs retain the genuine counterexample setup,
actual local A₆ action, Sylow flag, abelian conjugate span and H∈Hz, together
with universal earlier 13.7.6 and centralizer statements. The section is
marked by the intrinsic K/O₂(K) equivalence and its actual conjugation action.

The literal section gives a covering projection once U_H=[U_H,K]. Its kernel
is proved central and its source is generated by component commutators. The
concrete A₆ cover comparison yields the natural or five-dimensional
augmentation module; vanishing of H¹ for natural A₇ gives its natural module.
The product H=KT proves relative component normality, and the transvection
extends the component identifications to the full S₆ or S₇ action. In the
linear case the actual PSL₄(2) equivalence lifts to H=KT by absorbing O₂(H)
into the Sylow subgroup. Every full-module equivalence uses its actor model.

The assembly retains actual local A₆ or hexacode group equivalences. It
transfers the two noncentral L₁-chief factors from U_H through the actual
order-two line to U_H/V₁. Component recognition and proofs of the universal
earlier statements remain with their source-theorem owners; this module
proves the stated conditional section-to-model contract.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
13.7.6(1),(3), printed pp.938–940; I.1.5–6, p.408; and 13.8.5, pp.947–948.
-/
